Glyph — provenance and third-party notices
==========================================

Glyph is a new, clean implementation. No bootLogo source code is copied into
it. Its LOGO control model (FD/BK/RT/LT, PU/PD, REPEAT with bracketed
lists, TO ... END, CLEARSCREEN, SETCOLOR) and its draw-then-advance turtle
stepping were taken from the behaviour and documentation of bootLogo:

  nanochess/bootLogo — https://github.com/nanochess/bootLogo
  inspected at commit e3ce458a6d4eb0c0f41e3fc0f1239e09864b9df0
  (bootlogo.asm blob 0a0fc1b5, README.md blob b174f535, LICENSE blob fcbda331)

The conformance test tests/corpus/logo_bootlogo_flower.glyph reproduces the
example program from the bootLogo README. bootLogo's licence:

